{
  "about": "Inputs for trace-zone-polygons.mjs. Seeds only decide WHICH painted region of the client continent art belongs to a zone; the polygon edges come from the painted borders. Seed positions are well-known town/landmark spots in WoW server coordinates [X north, Y west] (approximate, +-200 yd; snapped to a calm pixel). Optional \"logged\" seeds are exact positions the client reported inside that zone, used unsnapped where the art's continent lettering hides a border. Telemetry stores the same point as world_x = Y, world_y = X. worldRect is the zone map's extent from the classic client's WorldMapArea table [left Y, right Y, top X, bottom X]; 10 of them (every zone our telemetry has visited) were checked against real samples (max error 0.0001 of the zone map). A zone polygon may not leave its rect.",
